newfs_udf/makefs -t udf: over-long file names wrap the one-byte l_fi

unix_to_udf_name stores the encoded length (1 + n, or 1 + 2n with any
character above U+00FF) in fid->l_fi, a uint8_t, without a check: 255 Latin-1
characters give l_fi = 0 (unreadable image), 128 wide ones a wrong name, while
makefs exits 0. Refuse such names.

Against NetBSD src 477d71b4d1b73a66b61a03b5f6d3dc9212d4f888 (sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c v1.14). Apply with patch -p1
in the src tree. Details: BUG-REPORT.md, bug 3.

--- a/sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c
+++ b/sbin/newfs_udf/udf_core.c
@@ -764,6 +764,10 @@
 		strncpy(result, name + 1, name_len);
 		udf_chars += name_len;
 	}
+	/* l_fi is one byte: a longer name would wrap and corrupt the directory */
+	if (udf_chars > 255)
+		errx(EXIT_FAILURE, "file name too long for UDF (%d bytes encoded, at most 255): %.*s",
+		    udf_chars, name_len, name);
 	*result_len = udf_chars;
 	free(raw_name);
 }
